    <lineage>
      <procstep>
        <procdesc>Field observations were submitted directly from field participants and consist of
          notes, descriptions, and measurements that document the existence and character of
          faulting or ground deformation at a geographic point. Observations of damage to buildings
          or earthen structures such as embankments or fills are not included in the compilation
          unless they reflect permanent deformation of the natural ground surface. All contributed
          site data were extracted from their originally provided formats, parsed, and loaded into a
          spatial database using a compilation schema developed by USGS and CGS. Each data record
          represents an observation of faulting, ground deformation or no deformation, that was made
          by an investigator or field team working together during a unique visit on a specific
          date. If the same observer/team revisits the same locality on a different day or time and
          records a separate observation, this constitutes a separate data record. Similarly,
          observations made by different field teams at the same locality are preserved as separate
          observation records. The goal of the compilation is to present the data as reported,
          interpreted only as necessary to assemble the information into the compilation schema and
          with as much metadata about the observation as possible.</procdesc>
